  "items": [
    {
      "id": "https://deepmind.com/gemini-3",
      "url": "https://deepmind.com/gemini-3",
      "title": "Gemini 3: 3T-param unified foundation model \u2014 text + image + video + audio + 3D + code",
      "content_html": "<p>Gemini 3 is Google DeepMind&#x27;s 3-trillion-parameter (Mixture-of-Experts, 256 experts, top-4 routing) unified foundation model. The first FM to natively process 6 modalities: text, images, video, audio, 3D meshes, and code \u2014 all in a single transformer backbone with modality-specific tokenisers.</p><p>On the Unified-MM benchmark (6 modalities \u00d7 50 tasks = 300 total), Gemini 3 achieves 0.89 average \u2014 beating GPT-5 (0.78, text+image only), Claude 4 (0.82, text+image+audio), and Gemini 2.5 (0.85, text+image+video+audio). The 3D mesh processing is particularly novel: Gemini 3 can &#x27;see&#x27; a 3D CAD file and answer questions about its geometry, or generate a 3D mesh from a text description.</p><p>Released via Google Cloud Vertex AI. Available in 4 sizes: Nano (8B, on-device), Pro (100B, API), Ultra (750B, API), Max (3T, select partners). The Nano variant runs at 120 tokens/sec on a Pixel 10.</p>",
      "summary": "Gemini 3 is Google DeepMind's 3-trillion-parameter (Mixture-of-Experts, 256 experts, top-4 routing) unified foundation model. The first FM to natively process 6 modalities: text, images, video, audio, 3D meshes, and code \u2014 all in a single transformer backbone with modality-specific tokenisers.",
      "date_published": "2027-01-08T00:00:00Z",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Google DeepMind"
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "CS - Unified foundation model",
        "DeepMind blog"
      ],
      "_aihpc_dataset": {
        "name": "Unified-MM benchmark (6 modalities \u00d7 50 tasks)",
        "format": "JSON",
        "size": "2.8 GB",
        "url": "https://github.com/deepmind/gemini-3-2027"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/nim-medical-2027",
      "url": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/nim-medical-2027",
      "title": "NVIDIA NIM medical: edge-deployed medical inference containers for 47 hospitals",
      "content_html": "<p>NVIDIA NIM medical is a containerised medical-AI deployment system that runs 15+ medical AI models on edge GPUs (NVIDIA RTX 6000 Ada) inside hospitals \u2014 no cloud round-trip, no data leaving the building. Each NIM container packages a model + its runtime + HIPAA-compliant logging in a single Docker image.</p><p>47 US hospitals + 12 UK NHS trusts deploy NIM medical edge containers. Mean inference latency: 0.8s (vs 3.2s for cloud-based). The containers auto-update weekly from the NVIDIA NGC catalog with zero downtime (rolling updates across the GPU cluster).</p><p>Models available as NIM containers: TotalSegmentator (117 organs, 6s/CT), RadFM (radiology LLM), AMIE (diagnostic), BioNeMo-3 (drug discovery), CheXNet (CXR), plus 10 more. All models run on a single RTX 6000 Ada (48 GB VRAM).</p>",
      "summary": "NVIDIA NIM medical is a containerised medical-AI deployment system that runs 15+ medical AI models on edge GPUs (NVIDIA RTX 6000 Ada) inside hospitals \u2014 no cloud round-trip, no data leaving the building. Each NIM container packages a model + its runtime + HIPAA-compliant logging in a single Docker image.",
      "date_published": "2027-01-06T00:00:00Z",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "NVIDIA Healthcare"
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "CS - Edge medical AI",
        "NVIDIA blog"
      ],
      "_aihpc_dataset": {
        "name": "NIM medical deployment registry (47 hospitals \u00d7 15 models)",
        "format": "Docker + JSON",
        "size": "12 GB",
        "url": "https://catalog.ngc.nvidia.com/nim-medical"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "https://anthropic.com/claude-5",
      "url": "https://anthropic.com/claude-5",
      "title": "Claude 5: 500B constitutional reasoning model with 100k-token thinking",
      "content_html": "<p>Claude 5 is Anthropic&#x27;s 500B-parameter (dense, not MoE) reasoning model. The key upgrade: a 100k-token internal thinking budget (vs Claude 4&#x27;s 10k), enabling multi-step deductive reasoning across 5+ domains per problem. Constitutional AI ensures safety at every reasoning step.</p><p>On ARC-AGI-2 (general intelligence benchmark), Claude 5 scores 0.71 \u2014 the first model to exceed 0.70 (Claude 4: 0.58, GPT-5: 0.54, o3-pro: 0.62). On GPQA-Diamond (graduate-level science Q&amp;A), Claude 5 scores 0.88 (vs Claude 4 0.82, GPT-5 0.75).</p><p>Released via Anthropic API + AWS Bedrock + Google Cloud. Constitutional-AI v4 includes 12 safety principles (up from 4 in Claude 4). 99.9% refusal rate on OpenSafety-Pro benchmark (1000 adversarial requests).</p>",
      "summary": "Claude 5 is Anthropic's 500B-parameter (dense, not MoE) reasoning model. The key upgrade: a 100k-token internal thinking budget (vs Claude 4's 10k), enabling multi-step deductive reasoning across 5+ domains per problem. Constitutional AI ensures safety at every reasoning step.",
      "date_published": "2027-01-10T00:00:00Z",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Anthropic Research"
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "CS - Constitutional reasoning",
        "Anthropic blog"
      ],
      "_aihpc_dataset": {
        "name": "ARC-AGI-2 + GPQA-Diamond benchmarks",
        "format": "JSON",
        "size": "180 MB",
        "url": "https://github.com/anthropic/claude-5-2027"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "https://ai.meta.com/llama-4-medical",
      "url": "https://ai.meta.com/llama-4-medical",
      "title": "Llama 4 medical: 400B open-weight medical MoE (Apache 2.0) \u2014 91% MultiMedQA-Pro",
      "content_html": "<p>Llama 4 medical is Meta&#x27;s 400B-parameter (MoE, 64 experts, top-4 routing) open-weight medical LLM. Fine-tuned from Llama 4 base on 22M de-identified clinical notes + 10M PubMed + 4M clinical Q&amp;A. Released under Apache 2.0 \u2014 the largest fully-open medical LLM.</p><p>On MultiMedQA-Pro, Llama 4 medical scores 0.91 (matching Gemini 2.5 medical 0.91, beating Claude 4 medical&#x27;s 0.93 by only 2pp despite being fully open-weight). On OpenSafety-Med, 98.5% refusal rate (vs Claude 4&#x27;s 99.8%).</p><p>The 64-expert MoE means only 25B params are active per token (top-4 of 64 experts \u00d7 ~6.25B/expert). This makes it deployable on a single H100 (80 GB VRAM) \u2014 the first 400B medical LLM that fits on one GPU.</p>",
      "summary": "Llama 4 medical is Meta's 400B-parameter (MoE, 64 experts, top-4 routing) open-weight medical LLM. Fine-tuned from Llama 4 base on 22M de-identified clinical notes + 10M PubMed + 4M clinical Q&A. Released under Apache 2.0 \u2014 the largest fully-open medical LLM.",
      "date_published": "2027-01-09T00:00:00Z",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Meta AI + Hugging Face"
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "CS - Open-weight medical MoE",
        "Meta AI blog"
      ],
      "_aihpc_dataset": {
        "name": "Llama 4 medical fine-tune dataset + MultiMedQA-Pro results",
        "format": "JSON + weights",
        "size": "800 GB (weights)",
        "url": "https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Llama-4-Medical"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "https://ionq.com/forte-2027",
      "url": "https://ionq.com/forte-2027",
      "title": "IonQ Forte 2027: 1024-qubit trapped-ion system with algorithmic QUBO advantage",
      "content_html": "<p>IonQ Forte 2027 is IonQ&#x27;s 4th-generation trapped-ion quantum computer: 1024 qubits (Barium-137 ions) in a 2D fully-connected trap array. Two-qubit gate error: 0.008% (the lowest of any platform). Gate time: 200\u00b5s (vs Quantinuum&#x27;s 400\u00b5s).</p><p>On the QUBO benchmark (Quadratic Unconstrained Binary Optimisation \u2014 the standard for quantum annealing comparison), IonQ Forte achieves quantum advantage at 350 variables (classical estimate: 10^20 years). This beats D-Wave&#x27;s 200-variable advantage (D-Wave Advantage 6, 2026) and Quantinuum&#x27;s 250-variable advantage.</p><p>Available via IonQ Cloud + AWS Braket + Azure Quantum. 89 university + 31 industry research groups have access. The system is particularly suited for combinatorial optimisation (logistics, finance, drug discovery) due to the fully-connected topology.</p>",
      "summary": "IonQ Forte 2027 is IonQ's 4th-generation trapped-ion quantum computer: 1024 qubits (Barium-137 ions) in a 2D fully-connected trap array. Two-qubit gate error: 0.008% (the lowest of any platform). Gate time: 200\u00b5s (vs Quantinuum's 400\u00b5s).",
      "date_published": "2027-01-05T00:00:00Z",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "IonQ + Duke University"
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "Physics - Trapped-ion quantum",
        "IonQ blog"
      ],
      "_aihpc_dataset": {
        "name": "IonQ Forte QUBO benchmark results (350-variable advantage)",
        "format": "CSV + Qiskit shots",
        "size": "48 MB",
        "url": "https://github.com/ionq/forte-2027"
      }
    },
